From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PickleHik3 <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] tl-launcherctl: the client of the launcher's HTTP API,
 and -Dlauncherctl

New feature option launcherctl (default auto). It is on when networkmanager and modemmanager are
both off, which is this build, and an error when it is enabled with either of them on: the
backends that follow replace the UPower, NetworkManager, ModemManager and iio-sensor-proxy ones
(the rotation manager's) and the torch manager's, and a build with launcherctl does not look
for upower-glib. It defines PHOSH_HAVE_LAUNCHERCTL and needs json-glib.

src/tl-launcherctl.[ch] is the one client the backends share (libsoup 3). The endpoint is read
from ~/.launcherctl/endpoint and the token from ~/.launcherctl/token on every connection and
every POST, and sent as a bearer token. ONE GET /v1/watch stream (server-sent events) is held
open; the launcher sends one event per topic when it opens, which is the state of each, and one
for each change, so no GET is made and nothing polls. Without the two files the client is
unavailable and does nothing more (no timer, no connection attempt). A stream that breaks or
stays silent for 45 s (the launcher keeps it alive every 15 s) is opened again after 2 s, 4 s,
8 s ... 60 s; an event resets that.

API (src/tl-launcherctl.h; also for the notify manager, which POSTs /v1/notify):

  TlLauncherctl *tl_launcherctl_get_default (void);  /* starts the stream on the first call */
  gboolean       tl_launcherctl_get_available (self);  /* the stream is open; notify::available */
  JsonObject    *tl_launcherctl_get_last (self, "battery"|"network"|"rotation");  /* or NULL */
  void           tl_launcherctl_post_async (self, "/v1/torch", "{\"on\":true}", cancellable,
                                            callback, user_data);
  JsonObject    *tl_launcherctl_post_finish (self, res, &error);  /* the reply's JSON object */
  signal "event" (detail = topic, arg JsonObject*): connect to "event::battery" and the like.
  JsonObject    *tl_json_get_object (object, "member");  /* quiet accessor, inline */

A POST finishes with an error when there is no endpoint or the launcher answers anything but 2xx,
so a notify manager closes a notification with
  tl_launcherctl_post_async (client, "/v1/notify", "{\"close\":\"<id>\"}", ...).
